{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"fetch","tool":"fetch","arguments":{"max_length":15000,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_international_trips_made_by_Xi_Jinping"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Contents of https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_international_trips_made_by_Xi_Jinping:\nFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\nThis is a **list of international trips made by Xi Jinping**, the [general secretary of the Chinese Communist Party](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Secretary_of_the_Chinese_Communist_Party \"General Secretary of the Chinese Communist Party\") and the [president of China](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_China \"President of China\"). [Xi Jinping](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xi_Jinping \"Xi Jinping\") has made 56 international trips to 71 countries since he assumed the [general secretaryship](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_secretaryship_of_Xi_Jinping \"General secretaryship of Xi Jinping\") on 15 November 2012 and the presidency on 14 March 2013. Xi's travels currently take place on a modified [Air China](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Air_China \"Air China\") [747-8](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boeing_747-8 \"Boeing 747-8\").\n\nThe number of visits per country where he has travelled are:\n\n* **One** visit to: Australia, Bangladesh, Belarus, Belgium, Brunei, Chile, Costa Rica, Cuba, Czech Republic, Ecuador, Egypt, Fiji, Finland, Hungary, Iran, Japan, Laos, Maldives, Mauritius, Mexico, Monaco, Mongolia, Morocco, Myanmar, Nepal, the Netherlands, New Zealand, Pakistan, Panama, Papua New Guinea, Poland, Republic of the Congo, Rwanda, Senegal, Singapore, Sri Lanka, Switzerland, Tanzania, Thailand, Trinidad and Tobago, Turkey, Turkmenistan, United Arab Emirates, United Kingdom, Venezuela, Zimbabwe.\n* **Two** visits to: Argentina, Cambodia, Germany, Greece, Italy, Kyrgyzstan, Malaysia, North Korea, Peru, Philippines, Portugal, Saudi Arabia, Serbia, South Korea, and Spain.\n* **Three** visits to: Brazil, India, Indonesia, Tajikistan, and Uzbekistan.\n* **Four** visits to: South Africa, France, and Vietnam.\n* **Five** visits to: the United States\n* **Six** visits to: Kazakhstan\n* **Eleven** visits to: Russia.\n\n[![](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/List_of_international_trips_made_by_Xi_Jinping.svg/960px-List_of_international_trips_made_by_Xi_Jinping.svg.png)](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:List_of_international_trips_made_by_Xi_Jinping.svg)\n\nWorld map highlighting countries visited by Xi Jinping during his leadership, as of July 2026.\n\n  One visit\n\n  Two visits\n\n  Three visits\n\n  Four visits\n\n  Five visits\n\n  Six visits\n\n  Seven or more visits\n\n  China\n\n|  | Dates | Country | Locations | Details | Image |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | 22–24 March | [Russia](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russia \"Russia\") | [Moscow](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moscow \"Moscow\") | [State visit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_visit_by_Xi_Jinping_to_Russia,_Tanzania,_South_Africa_and_Congo \"State visit by Xi Jinping to Russia, Tanzania, South Africa and Congo\"); His first foreign trip as China's [paramount leader](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paramount_leader \"Paramount leader\") and [state representative](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_state_representatives_of_the_People's_Republic_of_China \"List of state representatives of the People's Republic of China\"). Met with President [Vladimir Putin](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vladimir_Putin \"Vladimir Putin\") to discuss bilateral ties. Discussions of a new comprehensive strategic cooperation plan between China and Russia were held. Increased tourism cooperation and cultural ties were agreed upon.[[1]](#cite_note-1) Met with Chairman of the State Duma [Sergei Naryshkin](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sergei_Naryshkin \"Sergei Naryshkin\") to discuss enhancement of inter-parliamentary ties between China and Russia.[[2]](#cite_note-2) Met with Russian Defense Minister [Sergei Shoigu](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sergei_Shoigu \"Sergei Shoigu\") to discuss increased military ties between China and Russia.[[3]](#cite_note-3) Met with Russian Minister of Far East Development [Viktor Ishayev](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viktor_Ishayev \"Viktor Ishayev\") to discuss increased economic cooperation in the Russian Far East.[[4]](#cite_note-4) |  |\n| 24–25 March | [Tanzania](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tanzania \"Tanzania\") | [Dar es Salaam](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dar_es_Salaam \"Dar es Salaam\") | [State visit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_visit_by_Xi_Jinping_to_Russia,_Tanzania,_South_Africa_and_Congo \"State visit by Xi Jinping to Russia, Tanzania, South Africa and Congo\"); Met with President of Tanzania [Jakaya Mrisho Kikwete](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jakaya_Mrisho_Kikwete \"Jakaya Mrisho Kikwete\") to discuss bilateral ties. A joint communique was signed on boosting friendly cooperation between China and Tanzania.[[5]](#cite_note-5) Met with President of Zanzibar [Ali Mohamed Shein](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ali_Mohamed_Shein \"Ali Mohamed Shein\") to discuss bilateral ties.[[6]](#cite_note-6) |  |\n| 25–29 March | [South Africa](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Africa \"South Africa\") | [Pretoria](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pretoria \"Pretoria\"), [Durban](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Durban \"Durban\") | [State visit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_visit_by_Xi_Jinping_to_Russia,_Tanzania,_South_Africa_and_Congo \"State visit by Xi Jinping to Russia, Tanzania, South Africa and Congo\") and attendance to the [5th BRICS summit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/5th_BRICS_summit \"5th BRICS summit\").[[7]](#cite_note-7)[[8]](#cite_note-russiaafrica2-8) |  |\n| 29–30 March | [Republic of the Congo](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republic_of_the_Congo \"Republic of the Congo\") | [Brazzaville](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brazzaville \"Brazzaville\") | [State visit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_visit_by_Xi_Jinping_to_Russia,_Tanzania,_South_Africa_and_Congo \"State visit by Xi Jinping to Russia, Tanzania, South Africa and Congo\"); Met with President [Denis Sassou Nguesso](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denis_Sassou_Nguesso \"Denis Sassou Nguesso\") to discuss bilateral ties. Talks were held to improve cooperation between Chinese doctors and African health services.[[9]](#cite_note-9)[[8]](#cite_note-russiaafrica2-8) |  |\n| 2 | 31 May–2 June | [Trinidad and Tobago](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trinidad_and_Tobago \"Trinidad and Tobago\") | [Port of Spain](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Port_of_Spain \"Port of Spain\") | Met with President of Trinidad and Tobago [Anthony Carmona](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anthony_Carmona \"Anthony Carmona\") and Prime Minister of Trinidad and Tobago [Kamla Persad-Bissessar](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kamla_Persad-Bissessar \"Kamla Persad-Bissessar\") to discuss bilateral ties.[[10]](#cite_note-10) Met with Trinidad and Tobago Senate President [Timothy Hamel-Smith](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timothy_Hamel-Smith \"Timothy Hamel-Smith\") and Speaker of the House [Wade Mark](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wade_Mark \"Wade Mark\") to discuss increased legislative exchanges between China and Trinidad and Tobago.[[11]](#cite_note-11) Met with President of Guyana [Donald Ramotar](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Ramotar \"Donald Ramotar\") to discuss bilateral ties.[[12]](#cite_note-12) Met with President of Suriname [Dési Bouterse](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dési_Bouterse \"Dési Bouterse\") to discuss bilateral ties.[[13]](#cite_note-13) |  |\n| 2–4 June | [Costa Rica](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Costa_Rica \"Costa Rica\") | [San José](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_José,_Costa_Rica \"San José, Costa Rica\") | [[14]](#cite_note-14) |  |\n| 4–7 June | [Mexico](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mexico \"Mexico\") | [Mexico City](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mexico_City \"Mexico City\") | [[15]](#cite_note-15) |  |\n| 7–9 June | [United States](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States \"United States\") | [Ontario, California](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ontario,_California \"Ontario, California\") [Rancho 