te-Perlez-2019-114) See [Kim–Xi meetings](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kim–Xi_meetings \"Kim–Xi meetings\").[[115]](#cite_note-:9-115) |  |\n| 5 | 27–29 June | [Japan](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Japan \"Japan\") | [Osaka](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Osaka \"Osaka\") | Attendance to the [14th G20 summit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2019_G20_Osaka_summit \"2019 G20 Osaka summit\"). Met with U.S. President [Donald Trump](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Donald_Trump \"Donald Trump\").[[116]](#cite_note-116) |  |\n| 6 | 11–12 October | [India](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India \"India\") | [Chennai](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chennai \"Chennai\") [Mahabalipuram](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahabalipuram \"Mahabalipuram\") | Informal summit with Prime Minister [Narendra Modi](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narendra_Modi \"Narendra Modi\"). |  |\n| 12–13 October | [Nepal](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nepal \"Nepal\") | [Kathmandu](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kathmandu \"Kathmandu\") | State visit. |  |\n| 7 | 10–12 November | [Greece](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greece \"Greece\") | [Athens](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Athens \"Athens\") | State visit. |  |\n| 12–14 November | [Brazil](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brazil \"Brazil\") | [Brasília](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brasília \"Brasília\") | Attendance to the [11th BRICS summit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/11th_BRICS_summit \"11th BRICS summit\"). Met with President [Jair Bolsonaro](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jair_Bolsonaro \"Jair Bolsonaro\"). |  |\n\n|  | Dates | Country | Locations | Details | Image |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | 17–18 January | [Myanmar](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myanmar \"Myanmar\") | [Nay Pyi Taw](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nay_Pyi_Taw \"Nay Pyi Taw\") | State visit. Met President [Win Myint](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Win_Myint \"Win Myint\"), State Councillor [Aung San Suu Kyi](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aung_San_Suu_Kyi \"Aung San Suu Kyi\") and military leader [Min Aung Hlaing](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Min_Aung_Hlaing \"Min Aung Hlaing\").[[117]](#cite_note-117) |  |\n\nBetween 2020 and 2022, Xi paused foreign travel, speculated to be due to the COVID-19 pandemic.[[118]](#cite_note-118)\n\n|  | Dates | Country | Locations | Details | Image |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | 14 September | [Kazakhstan](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kazakhstan \"Kazakhstan\") | [Nur-Sultan](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nur-Sultan \"Nur-Sultan\") | [State visit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_state_visit_by_Xi_Jinping_to_Kazakhstan_and_Uzbekistan \"2022 state visit by Xi Jinping to Kazakhstan and Uzbekistan\"). Xi's first visit outside China since January 2020, the start of the [COVID-19 pandemic](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COVID-19_pandemic_in_China \"COVID-19 pandemic in China\"). Met with President [Kassym-Jomart Tokayev](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kassym-Jomart_Tokayev \"Kassym-Jomart Tokayev\").[[119]](#cite_note-119) |  |\n| 14–16 September | [Uzbekistan](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uzbekistan \"Uzbekistan\") | [Samarkand](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samarkand \"Samarkand\") | [State visit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_state_visit_by_Xi_Jinping_to_Kazakhstan_and_Uzbekistan \"2022 state visit by Xi Jinping to Kazakhstan and Uzbekistan\") and attendance to [2022 Samarkand SCO summit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Samarkand_SCO_summit \"2022 Samarkand SCO summit\"). Met with Central Asian leaders as well as Russian president Vladimir Putin, his first since Russia invaded Ukraine on 24 February 2022.[[120]](#cite_note-120)[[121]](#cite_note-121) |  |\n| 2 | 14–17 November | [Indonesia](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indonesia \"Indonesia\") | [Bali](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bali \"Bali\") | Attendance to the [17th G20 summit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_G20_Bali_summit \"2022 G20 Bali summit\"). Met numerous world leaders including the US president [Joe Biden](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joe_Biden \"Joe Biden\"), Australian Prime Minister [Anthony Albanese](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anthony_Albanese \"Anthony Albanese\"), French President [Emmanuel Macron](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emmanuel_Macron \"Emmanuel Macron\")[[122]](#cite_note-122) and South Korean president [Yoon Suk-yeol](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoon_Suk-yeol \"Yoon Suk-yeol\").[[123]](#cite_note-123)[[124]](#cite_note-124) |  |\n| 17–19 November | [Thailand](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thailand \"Thailand\") | [Bangkok](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bangkok \"Bangkok\") | State visit and attendance to the [APEC Thailand 2022](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/APEC_Thailand_2022 \"APEC Thailand 2022\"). Met with leaders including Japanese Prime Minister [Fumio Kishida](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fumio_Kishida \"Fumio Kishida\"),[[125]](#cite_note-125) New Zealand Prime Minister [Jacinda Ardern](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jacinda_Ardern \"Jacinda Ardern\"),[[126]](#cite_note-126) Thai Prime Minister [Prayut Chan-o-cha](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prayut_Chan-o-cha \"Prayut Chan-o-cha\")[[127]](#cite_note-127) and US Vice President [Kamala Harris](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kamala_Harris \"Kamala Harris\").[[128]](#cite_note-128) |  |\n| 3 | 7–10 December | [Saudi Arabia](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saudi_Arabia \"Saudi Arabia\") | [Riyadh](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riyadh \"Riyadh\") | State visit and attendance to the [China-Arab States Summit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_China-Arab_States_Summit \"2022 China-Arab States Summit\") and China-GCC Summit. Met king [Salman](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salman_of_Saudi_Arabia \"Salman of Saudi Arabia\"), and crown prince and prime minister [Mohammed bin Salman](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohammed_bin_Salman \"Mohammed bin Salman\"). Xi also met with numerous Arab leaders, including members of the [Gulf Cooperation Council](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gulf_Cooperation_Council \"Gulf Cooperation Council\").[[129]](#cite_note-129) During the meeting, he signed numerous commercial deals with Saudi Arabia and formally elevated the relationship to comprehensive strategic partnership, highest level in China's formal ranking of relations with other countries.[[130]](#cite_note-130) |  |\n\n|  | Dates | Country | Locations | Details | Image |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | 20–22 March | [Russia](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russia \"Russia\") | [Moscow](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moscow \"Moscow\") | [State visit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_visit_by_Xi_Jinping_to_Russia \"2023 visit by Xi Jinping to Russia\"). Second meeting with Putin after the [Russian invasion of Ukraine](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine_(2022–present) \"Russian invasion of Ukraine (2022–present)\"),[[131]](#cite_note-:1-131)[[132]](#cite_note-:2-132) as well as his first trip overseas after the [2023 National People's Congress](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_National_People's_Congress \"2023 National People's Congress\"). The visited came at the backdrop of [Russia's invasion of Ukraine](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine \"Russian invasion of Ukraine\"), as well as an arrest warrant for Putin issued by the [International Criminal Court](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Criminal_Court \"International Criminal Court\").[[133]](#cite_note-:6-133) During the visit, Xi met with Putin, as well as Prime Minister [Mikhail Mishustin](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mikhail_Mishustin \"Mikhail Mishustin\").[[134]](#cite_note-:3-134) Putin and Xi signed a joint statement vowing to expand ties, and officially promoted a new \"multipolar world\".[[133]](#cite_note-:6-133) |  |\n| 2 | 21–24 August | [South Africa](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Africa \"South Africa\") | [Pretoria](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pretoria \"Pretoria\") [Johannesburg](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johannesburg \"Johannesburg\") | State visit and attendance to the [15th BRICS summit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/15th_BRICS_summit \"15th BRICS summit\").[[135]](#cite_note-:4-135) Met with various BRICS leaders, as well as various leaders from the African continent.[[136]](#cite_note-:5-136) |  |\n| 3 | 14–17 November | [United States](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States \"United States\") | [San Francisco](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Francisco \"San Francisco\") | Attendance to the US-China leader summit and the [APEC United States 2023](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/APEC_United_States_2023 \"APEC United States 2023\").[[137]](#cite_note-:7-137) |  |\n| 4 | 12–13 December | [Vietnam](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vietnam \"Vietnam\") | [Hanoi](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hanoi \"Hanoi\") | [State visit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_state_visit_by_Xi_Jinping_to_Vietnam \"2023 state visit by Xi Jinping to Vietnam\").[[138]](#cite_note-:8-138) |  |\n\n|  | Dates | Country | Locations | Details | Image |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | 5–7 May | [France](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/France \"France\") | [Paris](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paris \"Paris\") [Tarbes](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarbes \"Tarbes\") | [State visit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_visits_by_Xi_Jinping_to_France,_Serbia_and_Hungary \"State visits by Xi Jinping to France, Serbia and Hungary\"). Met with French president [Emmanuel Macron](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emmanuel_Macron \"Emmanuel Macron\") and [European Commission](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_Commission \"European Commission\") President [Ursula von der Leyen](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ursula_von_der_Leyen \"Ursula von der Leyen\").[[139]](#cite_note-w644-139) |  |\n| 7–8 May | [Serbia](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Serbia \"Serbia\") | [Belgrade](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belgrade \"Belgrade\") | [State visit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_visits_by_Xi_Jinping_to_France,_Serbia_and_Hungary \"State visits by Xi Jinping to France, Serbia and Hungary\")[[139]](#cite_note-w644-139) |  |\n| 8–10 May | [Hungary](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hungary \"Hungary\") | [Budapest](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Budapest \"Budapest\") | [State visit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_visits_by_Xi_Jinping_to_France,_Serbia_and_Hungary \"State visits by Xi Jinping to France, Serbia and Hungary\")[[139]](#cite_note-w644-139) |  |\n| 2 | 2–4 July | [Kazakhstan](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kazakhstan \"Kazakhstan\") | [Astana](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astana \"Astana\") | [State visit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_state_visit_by_Xi_Jinping_to_Kazakhstan_and_Tajikistan \"2024 state visit by Xi Jinping to Kazakhstan and Tajikistan\") and attendance to the [2024 SCO summit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_SCO_summit \"2024 SCO summit\").[[140]](#cite_note-k216-140) |  |\n| 4–6 July | [Tajikistan](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tajikistan \"Tajikistan\") | [Dushanbe](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dushanbe \"Dushanbe\") | [State visit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_state_visit_by_Xi_Jinping_to_Kazakhstan_and_Tajikistan \"2024 state visit by Xi Jinping to Kazakhstan and Tajikistan\")[[140]](#cite_note-k216-140) |  |\n| 3 | 22–24 October | [Russia](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russia \"Russia\") | [Kazan](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kazan \"Kazan\") | Attendance to the [16th BRICS summit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/16th_BRICS_summit \"16th BRICS summit\"). |  |\n| 4 | 14–17 November | [Peru](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peru \"Peru\") | [Lima](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lima \"Lima\") | Attendance to the [APEC Peru 2024](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/APEC_Peru_2024 \"APEC Peru 2024\").[[141]](#cite_note-:02-141) [State visit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_state_visit_by_Xi_Jinping_to_Peru_and_Brazil \"2024 state visit by Xi Jinping to Peru and Brazil\"). |  |\n| 17–21 November | [Brazil](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brazil \"Brazil\") | [Rio de Janeiro](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rio_de_Janeiro \"Rio de Janeiro\") & [Brasília](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brasília \"Brasília\") | Attendance to the [19th G20 summit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_G20_Rio_de_Janeiro_summit \"2024 G20 Rio de Janeiro summit\"). [State visit](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_state_visit_by_Xi_Jinping_to_Peru_and_Brazil \"2024 state visit by Xi Jinping to Peru and Brazil\").[[142]](#cite_note-o243-142) |  |\n| 21–22 November | [Morocco](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morocco \"Morocco\") | [Casablanca](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casab