{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_48","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"fetch","tool":"fetch","arguments":{"max_length":15000,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_in_China#January%E2%80%93February"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Contents of https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_in_China#January%E2%80%93February:\nFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\n|  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| |  |  |  |  | | --- | --- | --- | --- | | ←   * [2022](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_in_China \"2022 in China\") * [2021](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2021_in_China \"2021 in China\") * [2020](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2020_in_China \"2020 in China\") * [2019](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2019_in_China \"2019 in China\") * [2018](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2018_in_China \"2018 in China\") |  | [2023](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AD_2023 \"AD 2023\")  in  [China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People's_Republic_of_China \"People's Republic of China\") | →   * [2024](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_in_China \"2024 in China\") * [2025](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_in_China \"2025 in China\") * [2026](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_in_China \"2026 in China\") * [2027](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2027_in_China \"2027 in China\") * [2028](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AD_2028 \"AD 2028\") | | |\n| Decades: | * [2000s](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:2000s_in_China \"Category:2000s in China\") * [2010s](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:2010s_in_China \"Category:2010s in China\") * **[2020s](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Category:2020s_in_China \"Category:2020s in China\")** |\n| See also: | [Other events of 2023](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023 \"2023\") [History of China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_China \"History of China\")  •  [Timeline](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_Chinese_history \"Timeline of Chinese history\")  •  [Years](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_years_in_China \"List of years in China\") |\n\nEvents in the year **[2023](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023 \"2023\") in [China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China \"China\")**.\n\n* [General Secretary of the Chinese Communist Party](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Secretary_of_the_Chinese_Communist_Party \"General Secretary of the Chinese Communist Party\") – [Xi Jinping](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xi_Jinping \"Xi Jinping\")\n* [President](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_China \"President of China\") – [Xi Jinping](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xi_Jinping \"Xi Jinping\")\n* [Vice President](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vice_President_of_China \"Vice President of China\")\n  + [Wang Qishan](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wang_Qishan \"Wang Qishan\") (until 10 March 2023)\n  + [Han Zheng](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Han_Zheng \"Han Zheng\") (from 10 March 2023)\n* [Premier](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Premier_of_China \"Premier of China\")\n  + [Li Keqiang](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Li_Keqiang \"Li Keqiang\") (until 11 March 2023)\n  + [Li Qiang](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Li_Qiang \"Li Qiang\") (from 11 March 2023)\n* [Congress chairman](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chairman_of_the_Standing_Committee_of_the_National_People's_Congress \"Chairman of the Standing Committee of the National People's Congress\") – [Li Zhanshu](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Li_Zhanshu \"Li Zhanshu\")\n* [Consultative Conference chairman](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chairman_of_the_National_Committee_of_the_Chinese_People's_Political_Consultative_Conference \"Chairman of the National Committee of the Chinese People's Political Consultative Conference\") – [Wang Yang](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wang_Yang_(politician) \"Wang Yang (politician)\")\n* [Supervision Commission director](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Director_of_the_National_Supervisory_Commission \"Director of the National Supervisory Commission\") – [Yang Xiaodu](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yang_Xiaodu \"Yang Xiaodu\")\n\n* 8 January – 17 people are killed and 22 others injured when a truck hits a [funeral procession](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Funeral_procession \"Funeral procession\") in [Nanchang County](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nanchang_County \"Nanchang County\"), [Jiangxi](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jiangxi \"Jiangxi\").[[1]](#cite_note-1)\n* 11 January – [2023 Guangzhou car attack](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Guangzhou_car_attack \"2023 Guangzhou car attack\"): Five people are killed and 13 others injured when a man [rams his vehicle](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vehicle-ramming_attack \"Vehicle-ramming attack\") into a crowd in [Guangzhou](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guangzhou \"Guangzhou\"), [Guangdong](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guangdong \"Guangdong\").[[2]](#cite_note-2)\n* 17 January – [2023 Nyingchi avalanche](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Nyingchi_avalanche \"2023 Nyingchi avalanche\"): An [avalanche](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Avalanche \"Avalanche\") in [Nyingchi](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nyingchi \"Nyingchi\"), [Tibet](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tibet \"Tibet\"), kills 28 people.[[3]](#cite_note-3)\n* 4 February – At least 16 people are killed and 66 others injured in a [multiple-vehicle collision](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multiple-vehicle_collision \"Multiple-vehicle collision\") along a highway in [Changsha](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Changsha \"Changsha\"), [Hunan](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hunan \"Hunan\").[[4]](#cite_note-4)\n* 12 February – [2023 Shandong high-altitude object](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Shandong_high-altitude_object \"2023 Shandong high-altitude object\"): China said that it detected an [unidentified flying object](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unidentified_flying_object \"Unidentified flying object\") over the [Yellow Sea](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow_Sea \"Yellow Sea\"), and warns that it is prepared to shoot it down. The Qingdao Marine Development Bureau issues an alert to fishermen in the waters to be \"on alert\" and \"avoid risks\".[[5]](#cite_note-5)\n* 22 February – [Alxa Left Banner mine collapse](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alxa_Left_Banner_mine_collapse \"Alxa Left Banner mine collapse\"): 53 people are killed by a [collapse](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mining_accident \"Mining accident\") at a [coal mine](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coal_mining \"Coal mining\") in [Alxa League](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alxa_League \"Alxa League\"), [Inner Mongolia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inner_Mongolia \"Inner Mongolia\").[[6]](#cite_note-6)\n* April – [India](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/India \"India\") surpasses China as the world's most populous country.[[7]](#cite_note-7)\n* 19 April – [2023 Beijing hospital fire](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Beijing_hospital_fire \"2023 Beijing hospital fire\"): Twenty-nine people are killed by a fire in a hospital in [Beijing](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beijing \"Beijing\").[[8]](#cite_note-BBC20230419-8)\n* 13 May – [Li Haoshi controversy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Li_Haoshi_controversy \"Li Haoshi controversy\")\n* 28 May – First flight of the [Comac C919](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comac_C919 \"Comac C919\"), China's first domestically made passenger aircraft, takes place between [Shanghai Hongqiao Airport](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shanghai_Hongqiao_Airport \"Shanghai Hongqiao Airport\") and [Beijing Capital Airport](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beijing_Capital_Airport \"Beijing Capital Airport\").[[9]](#cite_note-9)\n* 4 June – 19 people are killed by a [landslide](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Landslide \"Landslide\") at a mine in [Leshan](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leshan \"Leshan\") city of [Sichuan](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sichuan \"Sichuan\").[[10]](#cite_note-10)\n* 21 June – [2023 Yinchuan gas explosion](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Yinchuan_gas_explosion \"2023 Yinchuan gas explosion\"): At least 31 people are killed and seven injured by a [gas explosion](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gas_explosion \"Gas explosion\") at a barbecue restaurant in the city of [Yinchuan](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yinchuan \"Yinchuan\") in the northwest [Ningxia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ningxia \"Ningxia\") region. The [explosion](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Explosion \"Explosion\") was caused by a leak in a [liquefied gas](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liquefied_gas \"Liquefied gas\") tank inside the restaurant.[[11]](#cite_note-11)\n* 10 July – Six people, including three children, are killed and one injured in an early morning [knife attack at a kindergarten](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Lianjiang_stabbing \"2023 Lianjiang stabbing\") in [Lianjiang](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lianjiang,_Guangdong \"Lianjiang, Guangdong\"), Guangdong.[[12]](#cite_note-12)\n* 23 July – [2023 Qiqihar school gymnasium collapse](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Qiqihar_school_gymnasium_collapse \"2023 Qiqihar school gymnasium collapse\"): 11 people are killed by the collapse of a school gym in [Qiqihar](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qiqihar \"Qiqihar\"), [Heilongjiang](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heilongjiang \"Heilongjiang\").\n* 2 August – [Typhoon Doksuri](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Typhoon_Doksuri \"Typhoon Doksuri\") brings heavy rainfall to Beijing and [Hebei](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hebei \"Hebei\"). In [Changping](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Changping,_Beijing \"Changping, Beijing\"), it sets a maximum rainfall record since record-keeping began in 1883.[[13]](#cite_note-bj1-13) At least 80 people are killed and 35 missing by flooding in localities of Beijing, Hebei, [Jilin](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jilin \"Jilin\") and [Liaoning](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liaoning \"Liaoning\").[[14]](#cite_note-INDIATV-14)[[15]](#cite_note-15)\n* 11 August – 24 people are killed and 3 are missing after a [flash flood](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flash_flood \"Flash flood\") and [landslides](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Landslide \"Landslide\") in the village of Weiziping in [Chang'an](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chang'an,_Xi'an \"Chang'an, Xi'an\"), [Xi'an](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xi'an \"Xi'an\").[[16]](#cite_note-16)\n* 8 September – Flooding occurs in [Guangdong](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guangdong_Province \"Guangdong Province\") and [Fujian](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fujian_Province \"Fujian Province\") province in [southern China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southern_China \"Southern China\") after [Typhon Haikui](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Pacific_typhoon_season#Typhoon_Haikui_(Hanna) \"2023 Pacific typhoon season\") makes [landfall](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Landfall \"Landfall\") over the region. Rainfall in [Shenzhen](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shenzhen \"Shenzhen\") reaches record levels, the heaviest since meteorological records began in the city.[[17]](#cite_note-17)\n* 22 September – [Syrian President](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Syria \"President of Syria\") [Bashar al-Assad](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bashar_al-Assad \"Bashar al-Assad\") visits China, meets with [Chinese leader](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paramount_leader \"Paramount leader\") [Xi Jinping](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xi_Jinping \"Xi Jinping\"), and signs a strategic partnership with China on infrastructure as part of China's [Belt and Road Initiative](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belt_and_Road_Initiative \"Belt and Road Initiative\").[[18]](#cite_note-18)\n* 13 October – An [Israeli](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israel \"Israel\") [diplomat](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomat \"Diplomat\") based at the [Embassy of Israel, Beijing](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embassy_of_Israel,_Beijing \"Embassy of Israel, Beijing\") is stabbed by an unknown foreign attacker. The diplomat was taken to a hospital for treatment and is in stable condition. The incident is being treated as a [terrorist](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terrorism_in_China \"Terrorism in China\") attack.[[19]](#cite_note-19)\n* 16 October\n  + China will provide emergency [humanitarian aid](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Humanitarian_aid \"Humanitarian aid\") to the [UN Palestine agency](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UNRWA \"UNRWA\") and the [Palestinian Authority](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palestinian_Authority \"Palestinian Authority\"). The [CIDCA](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China_International_Development_Cooperation_Agency \"China International Development Cooperation Agency\") says the aid will be used to address urgent needs, such as food and medical care.[[20]](#cite_note-20)\n  + Former [Bank of China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bank_of_China \"Bank of China\") chair [Liu Lian'ge](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liu_Lian'ge \"Liu Lian'ge\") is arrested on allegations of [corruption](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corruption_in_China \"Corruption in China\").[[21]](#cite_note-21)\n* 17 October – [Hungarian Prime Minister](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_Hungary \"Prime Minister of Hungary\") [Viktor Orbán](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Viktor_Orb%C3%A1n \"Viktor Orbán\") and [Russian President](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Russia \"President of Russia\") [Vladimir Putin](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vladimir_Putin \"Vladimir Putin\") hold [talks](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diplomacy \"Diplomacy\") at the Belt and Road Initiative forum in Beijing. It is the first meeting between Putin and an [EU](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_Union \"European Union\") leader since [Russia's invasion of Ukraine](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine \"Russian invasion of Ukraine\").[[22]](#cite_note-22)\n* 24 October – The [Standing Committee of the National People's Congress of China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Standing_Committee_of_the_National_People's_Congress_of_China \"Standing Committee of the National People's Congress of China\") votes to remove several [SCtate Council](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_Council_of_China \"State Council of China\") members from their positions, including [defense minister](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minister_of_National_Defense_(China) \"Minister of National Defense (China)\") [Li Shangfu](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Li_Shangfu \"Li Shangfu\"), [finance minister](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ministry_of_Finance_(China) \"Ministry of Finance (China)\") [Liu Kun](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Liu_Kun \"Liu Kun\"), and [science minister](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ministry_of_Science_and_Technology_(China) \"Ministry of Science and Technology (China)\") [Wang Zhigang](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wang_Zhigang \"Wang Zhigang\").[[23]](#cite_note-23)\n* 10 November – China imposes \"control measures\" against [Philippine](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philippine \"Philippine\") vessels at a contested [South China Sea](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_China_Sea \"South China Sea\") location after a Philippine [auxiliary ship](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Auxiliary_ship \"Auxiliary ship\") entered the area which China deemed as infringing on its [sovereignty](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sovereignty \"Sovereignty\").[[24]](#cite_note-24)\n* 13 November – [2023 Chinese pneumonia outbreak](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Chinese_pneumonia_outbreak \"2023 Chinese pneumonia outbreak\"): [National Health Commission](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Health_Commission \"National Health Commission\") reports a [pneumonia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pneumonia \"Pneumonia\") outbreak in Beijing \n\n<error>Content truncated. Call the fetch tool with a start_index of 15000 to get more content.</error>"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
