{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"fetch","tool":"fetch","arguments":{"max_length":15000,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_visit_by_Xi_Jinping_to_Russia"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Contents of https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_visit_by_Xi_Jinping_to_Russia:\nFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\n2023 visit by Xi Jinping to Russia\n\n|  |  |\n| --- | --- |\n| Part of [China–Russia relations](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China%E2%80%93Russia_relations \"China–Russia relations\"), [Russo-Ukrainian War](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_War \"Russo-Ukrainian War\") | |\n| Putin welcomes Xi to Moscow, 21 March 2023 | |\n| Date | 20–22 March 2023 |\n| Location | * [Moscow](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moscow \"Moscow\"), Russia |\n| Participants | [Xi Jinping](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xi_Jinping \"Xi Jinping\") [Vladimir Putin](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vladimir_Putin \"Vladimir Putin\") |\n\nOn 20–22 March 2023, [Xi Jinping](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xi_Jinping \"Xi Jinping\"), [general secretary of the Chinese Communist Party](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Secretary_of_the_Chinese_Communist_Party \"General Secretary of the Chinese Communist Party\") and [Chinese president](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_China \"President of China\"), visited [Russia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russia \"Russia\"), in his first [international meeting](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_international_trips_made_by_Xi_Jinping \"List of international trips made by Xi Jinping\") since his [re-election](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_People's_Republic_of_China_presidential_election \"2023 People's Republic of China presidential election\") as president during the [2023 National People's Congress](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_National_People's_Congress \"2023 National People's Congress\").[[1]](#cite_note-o267-1)\n\nDuring the talks, the two sides signed a joint statement.[[2]](#cite_note-w286-2) The two sides stated that they should strengthen overall design and top-level planning, expand trade in energy, resources and electromechanical products, enhance the resilience of the industrial chain supply chain between the two sides, expand cooperation in the fields of information technology, digital economy, agriculture and trade in services, and push forward the complementary and synchronized development of cooperation in traditional trade and emerging fields, as well as further smoothening [cross-border](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cross-border \"Cross-border\") logistics and transportation.[[3]](#cite_note-v287-3)[[4]](#cite_note-4) Xi said he has a [peace plan for Ukraine](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace_negotiations_in_the_Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine \"Peace negotiations in the Russian invasion of Ukraine\").[[5]](#cite_note-5)\n\nA few weeks before Xi's visit, China issued a paper outlining its positions regarding de-escalation and political settlement of the [Russo-Ukrainian war](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russo-Ukrainian_war \"Russo-Ukrainian war\").[[6]](#cite_note-6) The visit came just days after China won a major diplomatic victory, bringing [Iran](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran \"Iran\") and [Saudi Arabia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saudi_Arabia \"Saudi Arabia\") closer together and restoring their [diplomatic relations](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iran%E2%80%93Saudi_Arabia_relations \"Iran–Saudi Arabia relations\").[[7]](#cite_note-:0-7)\n\nHours after it was announced that [Xi Jinping](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xi_Jinping \"Xi Jinping\") would visit Russia, the [International Criminal Court](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Criminal_Court \"International Criminal Court\") issued a [warrant to arrest](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ICC_arrest_warrants_for_Vladimir_Putin_and_Maria_Lvova-Belova \"ICC arrest warrants for Vladimir Putin and Maria Lvova-Belova\") [Vladimir Putin](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vladimir_Putin \"Vladimir Putin\").[[7]](#cite_note-:0-7)\n\nPrior to the visit, Xi Jinping and Vladimir Putin published separate articles;[[8]](#cite_note-e626-8) Xi said China's proposal to end the [Russo-Ukrainian War](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine_(2022%E2%80%93present) \"Russian invasion of Ukraine (2022–present)\") reflected world opinion. Putin said he had high hopes for the visit of his \"good old friend.\"[[9]](#cite_note-9) [Wang Wenbin](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wang_Wenbin \"Wang Wenbin\"), the spokesman for the [Ministry of Foreign Affairs](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ministry_of_Foreign_Affairs_(China) \"Ministry of Foreign Affairs (China)\"), described Xi Jinping's visit to Russia as a \"friendship tour\", \"cooperation tour\" and \"peace tour\" at a regular press conference. He will also exchange views on international and regional issues of concern to both countries and promote strategic collaboration and cooperation.[[10]](#cite_note-y038-10)\n\n[![](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Putin-Xi_meeting_%282023%29_5.jpg/250px-Putin-Xi_meeting_%282023%29_5.jpg)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Putin-Xi_meeting_(2023)_5.jpg)\n\nXi Jinping and Vladimir Putin before the beginning of Russian-Chinese talks on March 21, 2023\n\nOn the morning of March 20, 2023, President Xi Jinping arrived at [Moscow](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moscow \"Moscow\")'s [Vnukovo International Airport](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vnukovo_International_Airport \"Vnukovo International Airport\") on a special plane and was greeted by [Deputy Prime Minister of the Russian Federation](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deputy_Chairman_of_the_Government \"Deputy Chairman of the Government\") [Dmitry Chernyshenko](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dmitry_Chernyshenko \"Dmitry Chernyshenko\").[[11]](#cite_note-h508-11) Chinese officials, including [Cai Qi](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cai_Qi \"Cai Qi\"), [Wang Yi](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wang_Yi_(politician) \"Wang Yi (politician)\"), and [Qin Gang](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qin_Gang \"Qin Gang\"), accompanied him on the visit.[[12]](#cite_note-u279-12)\n\nIn the afternoon, President Xi, who has just arrived in Moscow, met with [Russian president](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_president \"Russian president\") [Vladimir Putin](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vladimir_Putin \"Vladimir Putin\") at the [Kremlin](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kremlin \"Kremlin\"). The two heads of state had in-depth and frank exchanges on [China–Russia relations](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China%E2%80%93Russia_relations \"China–Russia relations\"), national development, and issues of common concern in Ukraine.[[13]](#cite_note-v193-13) During Xi Jinping's visit, Vladimir Putin said Russia is ready to discuss China's initiative for [ending the conflict in Ukraine](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peace_negotiations_in_the_Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine \"Peace negotiations in the Russian invasion of Ukraine\"), adding that he had looked at China's proposals for a resolution of the Ukraine conflict and that he viewed them with respect.[[14]](#cite_note-14)[[15]](#cite_note-15)\n\n[![](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Putin-Xi_meeting_%282023%29_7.jpg/250px-Putin-Xi_meeting_%282023%29_7.jpg)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Putin-Xi_meeting_(2023)_7.jpg)\n\nRussia and China signed the package of documents\n\nOn the morning of March 21, President Xi met with [Russian prime minister](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_Russia \"Prime Minister of Russia\") [Mikhail Mishustin](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mikhail_Mishustin \"Mikhail Mishustin\") at the [Government House of the Russian Federation](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_House_(Moscow) \"White House (Moscow)\").[[16]](#cite_note-u277-16) On the afternoon of March 21, Xi Jinping held an official meeting with Vladimir Putin.[[17]](#cite_note-17) Following the meeting, Xi Jinping and Putin signed the Joint Declaration of the People's Republic of China and the Russian Federation on the Deepening of Comprehensive Strategic Collaboration and Partnership for the New Era and the president of the People's Republic of China and the president of the Russian Federation on the Development Plan of Priority Directions of China-Russia Economic Cooperation for the Period up to 2030.[[18]](#cite_note-p050-18) During the visit, the two sides also signed a number of bilateral cooperation documents in the fields of agriculture, forestry, basic scientific research, market regulation and media.[[3]](#cite_note-v287-3)\n\n[![](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Zaporizhzhia_after_Russian_shelling%2C_2023-03-22_%2801%29.webp/250px-Zaporizhzhia_after_Russian_shelling%2C_2023-03-22_%2801%29.webp.png)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Zaporizhzhia_after_Russian_shelling,_2023-03-22_(01).webp)\n\nResidential buildings in [Zaporizhzhia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zaporizhzhia \"Zaporizhzhia\") after [Russian rocket strikes](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022%E2%80%932023_Russian_strikes_against_Ukrainian_infrastructure \"2022–2023 Russian strikes against Ukrainian infrastructure\") on 22 March 2023, the second day of Xi's visit to Moscow\n\nOn the morning of March 22, President Xi left Moscow from Vnukovo International Airport on an Air China special flight, Russian Deputy Prime Minister [Chernyshenko](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dmitry_Chernyshenko \"Dmitry Chernyshenko\") and other high-ranking government officials were at the airport to see them off and held a grand send-off ceremony.[[19]](#cite_note-z856-19) The Russian military band played the Chinese military song \"[When That Day Comes](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/When_That_Day_Comes \"When That Day Comes\")\" to see him off.[[20]](#cite_note-20) Xi and his entourage returned to Beijing on the evening of March 22, Beijing time.[[21]](#cite_note-v148-21)\n\nXi Jinping's meeting with Putin was seen as [PR](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Public_relations \"Public relations\") victory for the Russian president amidst his increasing isolation. For China, the meeting served as a symbolic gesture of Beijing's refusal to conform to American dominance. Putin and Xi called each other \"dear friends\" and their body language was amicable. Putin praised the plan and blamed Ukraine and the West for rejecting it, while Xi Jinping avoided mentioning the conflict, refusing to make his stance clear.[[22]](#cite_note-22)\n\n[![](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/20230321ukraine_16.jpg/250px-20230321ukraine_16.jpg)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:20230321ukraine_16.jpg)\n\nFumio Kishida at [The Wall of Remembrance of the Fallen for Ukraine](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Wall_of_Remembrance_of_the_Fallen_for_Ukraine \"The Wall of Remembrance of the Fallen for Ukraine\") near [Mykhailivska Square](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mykhailivska_Square \"Mykhailivska Square\") in Kyiv on 21 March 2023\n\nOn the same day as this event, Japanese prime minister [Fumio Kishida](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fumio_Kishida \"Fumio Kishida\") [visited](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_visit_by_Fumio_Kishida_to_Ukraine \"2023 visit by Fumio Kishida to Ukraine\") [Volodymyr Zelenskyy](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Volodymyr_Zelenskyy \"Volodymyr Zelenskyy\") in Kyiv and visited [Bucha](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bucha,_Kyiv_Oblast \"Bucha, Kyiv Oblast\"), the site of the [2022 massacre](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bucha_massacre \"Bucha massacre\"). Kishida also stated that Russia's aggression against Ukraine is not just a European matter, but a challenge to the rules and principles of the entire international community.[[23]](#cite_note-23)\n\n[Valentina Matviyenko](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valentina_Matviyenko \"Valentina Matviyenko\"), [Chair of the Federation Council](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chairman_of_the_Federation_Council_(Russia) \"Chairman of the Federation Council (Russia)\"), posted, \"President Xi Jinping's trip is an epoch-making event in Russia-China bilateral relations. The visit proves the stability of high-level strategic collaboration between Russia and China.\"[[24]](#cite_note-w016-24)\n\nPolish prime minister [Mateusz Morawiecki](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mateusz_Morawiecki \"Mateusz Morawiecki\") expressed concern about a \"dangerous\" China-Russian alliance.[[25]](#cite_note-25)\n\n* [2024 visit by Vladimir Putin to China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_visit_by_Vladimir_Putin_to_China \"2024 visit by Vladimir Putin to China\")\n* [China–Russia relations](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China%E2%80%93Russia_relations \"China–Russia relations\")\n* [China and the Russian invasion of Ukraine](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China_and_the_Russian_invasion_of_Ukraine \"China and the Russian invasion of Ukraine\")\n* [List of international trips made by Xi Jinping](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_international_trips_made_by_Xi_Jinping \"List of international trips made by Xi Jinping\")\n* [2023 visit by Fumio Kishida to Ukraine](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_visit_by_Fumio_Kishida_to_Ukraine \"2023 visit by Fumio Kishida to Ukraine\")\n\n1. [↑](#cite_ref-o267_1-0) [\"路透社独家：习近平下周就将出访莫斯科 – DW – 2023年3月13日\"](https://www.dw.com/zh/%E8%B7%AF%E9%80%8F%E7%A4%BE%E7%8B%AC%E5%AE%B6%E4%B9%A0%E8%BF%91%E5%B9%B3%E4%B8%8B%E5%91%A8%E5%B0%B1%E5%B0%86%E5%87%BA%E8%AE%BF%E8%8E%AB%E6%96%AF%E7%A7%91/a-64970037). *dw.com* (in Chinese). 2023-03-13. Retrieved 2024-05-08.\n2. [↑](#cite_ref-w286_2-0) Rizzi, Andrea; Abril, Guillermo; Cuesta, Javier G. (2023-03-27). [\"Xi and Putin's plan for a 'new era': How to read between the lines\"](https://english.elpais.com/international/2023-03-27/xi-and-putins-plan-for-a-new-era-how-to-read-between-the-lines.html). *EL PAÍS English*. Retrieved 2024-05-10.\n3. [1](#cite_ref-v287_3-0) [2](#cite_ref-v287_3-1) [\"时政新闻眼丨习主席第9次访俄，取得哪些重要成果？\"](http://politics.people.com.cn/n1/2023/0322/c1001-32649240.html). *politics.people.com.cn* (in Chinese). 2023-03-22. Retrieved 2024-05-08.\n4. [↑](#cite_ref-4) [\"Joint Statement of the Russian Federation and the People's Republic of China on the International Relations Entering a New Era and the Global Sustainable Development\"](http://en.kremlin.ru/supplement/5770). *President of Russia*. Retrieved 10 May 2024.\n5. [↑](#cite_ref-5) [\"Peace plans and pipelines: What came out of the Putin-Xi talks?\"](https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/peace-plans-pipelines-what-came-out-putin-xi-talks-2023-03-22/). *Reuters*. 22 March 2023.\n6. [↑](#cite_ref-6) [\"China calls for a cease-fire and peace talks between Russia and Ukraine\"](https://web.archive.org/web/20230321193019/https://www.npr.org/2023/02/24/1159208413/china-calls-for-a-cease-fire-and-peace-talks-between-russia-and-ukraine). *[NPR](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NPR \"NPR\")*. 2023-02-24. Archived from [the original](https://www.npr.org/2023/02/24/1159208413/china-calls-for-a-cease-fire-and-peace-talks-between-russia-and-ukraine) on 2023-03-21. Retrieved 2023-02-26.\n7. [1](#cite_ref-:0_7-0) [2](#cite_ref-:0_7-1) Gan, Nectar (2023-03-20). [\"Xi makes 'journey of friendship' to Moscow days after Putin's war crime warrant issued\"](https://edition.cnn.com/2023/03/20/china/china-xi-putin-russia-visit-analysis-intl-hnk-mic/index.html). *[CNN](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CNN \"CNN\")*. [Archived](https://web.archive.org/web/20230321195643/https://editio\n\n<error>Content truncated. Call the fetch tool with a start_index of 15000 to get more content.</error>"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
