{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"fetch","tool":"fetch","arguments":{"max_length":12000,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Li_Shangfu"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Contents of https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Li_Shangfu:\nFrom Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia\n\n| Li Shangfu | |\n| --- | --- |\n| 李尚福 | |\n| Li in 2023 | |\n|  | |\n| [State Councilor of China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_councillor \"State councillor\") | |\n| **In office** 12 March 2023 – 24 October 2023 Serving with [Wang Xiaohong](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wang_Xiaohong \"Wang Xiaohong\"), [Wu Zhenglong](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wu_Zhenglong \"Wu Zhenglong\"), [Shen Yiqin](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shen_Yiqin \"Shen Yiqin\"), and [Qin Gang](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qin_Gang \"Qin Gang\") | |\n| Premier | [Li Qiang](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Li_Qiang \"Li Qiang\") |\n| 13th [Minister of National Defense](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minister_of_National_Defense_(China) \"Minister of National Defense (China)\") | |\n| **In office** 12 March 2023 – 24 October 2023 | |\n| Premier | Li Qiang |\n| CMC Chairman | [Xi Jinping](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xi_Jinping \"Xi Jinping\") |\n| Preceded by | [Wei Fenghe](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wei_Fenghe \"Wei Fenghe\") |\n| Succeeded by | [Dong Jun](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dong_Jun \"Dong Jun\") |\n| Head of the [Equipment Development Department](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equipment_Development_Department_of_the_Central_Military_Commission \"Equipment Development Department of the Central Military Commission\") | |\n| **In office** September 2017 – October 2022 | |\n| Preceded by | [Zhang Youxia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zhang_Youxia \"Zhang Youxia\") |\n| Succeeded by | [Xu Xueqiang](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xu_Xueqiang \"Xu Xueqiang\") |\n| Commander of the [China Manned Space Program](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China_Manned_Space_Program \"China Manned Space Program\") | |\n| **In office** September 2017 – October 2022 | |\n| Preceded by | Zhang Youxia |\n| Succeeded by | Xu Xueqiang |\n| Personal details | |\n| Born | February 1958 (age 68)  [Chengdu](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chengdu \"Chengdu\"), [Sichuan](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sichuan \"Sichuan\"), China |\n| [Party](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Political_party \"Political party\") | [Chinese Communist Party](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_Communist_Party \"Chinese Communist Party\") (1980–2024; expelled) |\n| [Alma mater](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alma_mater \"Alma mater\") | * [National University of Defense Technology](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_University_of_Defense_Technology \"National University of Defense Technology\") * [Chongqing University](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chongqing_University \"Chongqing University\") ([EngD](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doctor_of_Engineering \"Doctor of Engineering\")) |\n| Military service | |\n| Allegiance | [China](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/China \"China\") |\n| Branch/service | [People's Liberation Army Ground Force](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People's_Liberation_Army_Ground_Force \"People's Liberation Army Ground Force\")  [People's Liberation Army Strategic Support Force](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People's_Liberation_Army_Strategic_Support_Force \"People's Liberation Army Strategic Support Force\") |\n| Years of service | 1982–2024 |\n| Rank | [General](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jiang_(rank) \"Jiang (rank)\") (stripped in 2024) |\n|  | |\n\n**Li Shangfu** ([Chinese](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_language \"Chinese language\"): 李尚福; [pinyin](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pinyin \"Pinyin\"): *Lǐ Shàngfú*; born February 1958) is a Chinese [aerospace engineer](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aerospace_engineer \"Aerospace engineer\") and former military administrator. He served as the 13th [Minister of National Defense](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minister_of_National_Defense_(China) \"Minister of National Defense (China)\") and as [State Councillor](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_councillor \"State councillor\") of China from March to October 2023.\n\nLi joined the [People's Liberation Army](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People's_Liberation_Army \"People's Liberation Army\") (PLA) as a technician at the [Xichang Satellite Launch Center](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xichang_Satellite_Launch_Center \"Xichang Satellite Launch Center\") in 1982. He spent 31 years working at the Xichang Satellite Launch Center, including 10 years as the center director. Li Shangfu served as deputy director of the [PLA General Armaments Department](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People's_Liberation_Army_General_Armaments_Department \"People's Liberation Army General Armaments Department\") from 2014 to 2016 and director of the [Equipment Development Department](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equipment_Development_Department_of_the_Central_Military_Commission \"Equipment Development Department of the Central Military Commission\") of the [Central Military Commission](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_Military_Commission_(China) \"Central Military Commission (China)\") (CMC) from 2017 to 2022. He was conferred the rank of General in July 2019 and was appointed as a member of the CMC in October 2022. He was appointed as the 13th Minister of National Defense and as State Councillor in March 2023.\n\nIn August 2023, Li disappeared from public view and was then removed from office on October 24, 2023. He is both the shortest-serving Minister of National Defense and the first from the [PLA Strategic Support Force](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People's_Liberation_Army_Strategic_Support_Force \"People's Liberation Army Strategic Support Force\"). In June 2024, he was expelled from the [Chinese Communist Party](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_Communist_Party \"Chinese Communist Party\") (CCP) following corruption charges and his case transferred to the military's judiciary for criminal prosecution, and his rank of General revoked. In May 2026, Li was sentenced to [death with a two-year reprieve](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Death_sentence_with_reprieve \"Death sentence with reprieve\"), which will be commuted to life imprisonment without the possibility of parole upon the expiration of the two-year reprieve period.\n\nLi Shangfu was born in February 1958 in [Chengdu](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chengdu \"Chengdu\"), [Sichuan](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sichuan \"Sichuan\") Province, with his [ancestral home](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancestral_home_(Chinese) \"Ancestral home (Chinese)\") in [Xingguo County](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xingguo_County \"Xingguo County\"), [Jiangxi](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jiangxi \"Jiangxi\") Province. He is the son of [Li Shaozhu](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Li_Shaozhu \"Li Shaozhu\"), a [Red Army](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_Red_Army \"Chinese Red Army\") veteran and former high-ranking officer of the [PLA Railway Force](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PLA_Railway_Force?action=edit&redlink=1 \"PLA Railway Force (page does not exist)\") [[zh](https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E4%B8%AD%E5%9B%BD%E4%BA%BA%E6%B0%91%E8%A7%A3%E6%94%BE%E5%86%9B%E9%93%81%E9%81%93%E5%85%B5 \"zh:中国人民解放军铁道兵\")].[[1]](#cite_note-ifeng-1) Li Shangfu joined the PLA when he entered the [National University of Defense Technology](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_University_of_Defense_Technology \"National University of Defense Technology\") in 1978, and joined the CCP in June 1980. After graduating in 1982, he began working at the Xichang Satellite Launch Center as a technician.[[2]](#cite_note-chinadaily-2)[[3]](#cite_note-bio-3)\n\nLi attained a [Doctor of Engineering](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doctor_of_Engineering \"Doctor of Engineering\") in [control theory](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Control_theory \"Control theory\") and [control engineering](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Control_engineering \"Control engineering\") from [Chongqing University](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chongqing_University \"Chongqing University\").[[3]](#cite_note-bio-3)\n\nIn December 2003, he was promoted to Director (Commander) of the center at the age of 45. In 2006, he attained the rank of [major general](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Major_general \"Major general\").[[2]](#cite_note-chinadaily-2) In his ten years as director of the Xichang center, Li oversaw several rocket launches, including the launch of the [Chang'e 2](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chang'e_2 \"Chang'e 2\") lunar probe in October 2010.[[4]](#cite_note-4)\n\nAfter 31 years working in Xichang, Li was appointed [Chief of Staff](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chief_of_Staff \"Chief of Staff\") of the [PLA General Armaments Department](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People's_Liberation_Army_General_Armaments_Department \"People's Liberation Army General Armaments Department\") (GAD) in 2013, replacing Major General [Shang Hong](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shang_Hong \"Shang Hong\").[[1]](#cite_note-ifeng-1)[[2]](#cite_note-chinadaily-2) A year later, he was made deputy director of the GAD.[[2]](#cite_note-chinadaily-2)\n\n[![](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Zhang_Youxia_%282017-12-07%29_02.jpg/250px-Zhang_Youxia_%282017-12-07%29_02.jpg)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Zhang_Youxia_(2017-12-07)_02.jpg)\n\n[Zhang Youxia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zhang_Youxia \"Zhang Youxia\"), Li and the Chinese delegation in Moscow, Russia in 2017\n\nIn 2016, Li was appointed Deputy Commander of the newly established [PLA Strategic Support Force](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/People's_Liberation_Army_Strategic_Support_Force \"People's Liberation Army Strategic Support Force\"), which is responsible for cyberspace, space, and other high-tech warfare. He was promoted to the rank of lieutenant general in the same year.[[2]](#cite_note-chinadaily-2) In September 2017, Li was appointed Director of the [Equipment Development Department of the CMC](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Equipment_Development_Department_of_the_Central_Military_Commission \"Equipment Development Department of the Central Military Commission\"), the successor department of the GAD, replacing General [Zhang Youxia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zhang_Youxia \"Zhang Youxia\").[[2]](#cite_note-chinadaily-2)\n\nIn October 2017, Li was elected a member of the [19th CCP Central Committee](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/19th_Central_Committee_of_the_Chinese_Communist_Party \"19th Central Committee of the Chinese Communist Party\").[[5]](#cite_note-5)\n\nLi Shangfu was conferred the rank of major general in July 2006. In August 2016, he was conferred the rank of lieutenant general. In July 2019, he was conferred the rank of general.[[6]](#cite_note-6)\n\n### Central Military Commission\n\n[[edit](/w/index.php?title=Li_Shangfu&action=edit&section=3 \"Edit section: Central Military Commission\")]\n\nIn October 2022, he was nominated as a member of the 20th CMC of the CCP by Party general secretary [Xi Jinping](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Xi_Jinping \"Xi Jinping\").[[7]](#cite_note-:0-7) He ranked first among the members of the CMC.[[7]](#cite_note-:0-7)\n\nOn January 18, 2023, Li Shangfu attended the CMC promotion ceremony, and was appointed State Councilor and Minister of National Defense on March 12 of the same year, succeeding [Wei Fenghe](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wei_Fenghe \"Wei Fenghe\").[[8]](#cite_note-8) According to *[The Diplomat](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Diplomat_(magazine) \"The Diplomat (magazine)\")*, Li's promotion reflects Chinese attempts to prioritize aerospace in its defense modernization program, against a backdrop of increasing technological competition between China and the United States.[[9]](#cite_note-9)\n\n[![](//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/SCO_Defense_Ministers_meeting_%282023%29.jpg/250px-SCO_Defense_Ministers_meeting_%282023%29.jpg)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:SCO_Defense_Ministers_meeting_(2023).jpg)\n\nLi at the [SCO](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shanghai_Cooperation_Organisation \"Shanghai Cooperation Organisation\") defense ministers' meeting in New Delhi, India, 28 April 2023\n\nOn April 17, 2023, Li made his first overseas visit to Russia. As part of his four-day visit, he met with Russian president [Vladimir Putin](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vla\n\n<error>Content truncated. Call the fetch tool with a start_index of 12000 to get more content.</error>"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
