* *[De jure](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_jure \"De jure\")* ceasefire in effect since 10 October 2025 under second phase of [a peace deal](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaza_peace_plan \"Gaza peace plan\") * *[De facto](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_facto \"De facto\")* [limited war](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Limited_war \"Limited war\") | | Territorial changes | Approx. 64% of Gaza under Israeli military control as of April 2026[[1]](#cite_note-1) | | |\n| Belligerents | |\n| [Hamas](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamas \"Hamas\") [Palestinian allies](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palestinian_Joint_Operations_Room \"Palestinian Joint Operations Room\"), notably:  [Palestinian Islamic Jihad](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palestinian_Islamic_Jihad \"Palestinian Islamic Jihad\") | [Israel](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israel \"Israel\")[[a]](#cite_note-2) [Israeli-backed groups](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anti-Hamas_insurgency_in_Gaza \"Anti-Hamas insurgency in Gaza\"):   * + [Popular Forces](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Popular_Forces \"Popular Forces\")[[b]](#cite_note-7) |\n| Commanders and leaders | |\n| * [Hamas](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamas \"Hamas\") [Yahya Sinwar](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yahya_Sinwar \"Yahya Sinwar\") [**†**](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Killing_of_Yahya_Sinwar \"Killing of Yahya Sinwar\") * [Hamas](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamas \"Hamas\") [Ismail Haniyeh](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ismail_Haniyeh \"Ismail Haniyeh\") [**X**](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Assassination_of_Ismail_Haniyeh \"Assassination of Ismail Haniyeh\") * [Hamas](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamas \"Hamas\") [Mohammed Deif](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohammed_Deif \"Mohammed Deif\") [**X**](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/13_July_2024_al-Mawasi_attack \"13 July 2024 al-Mawasi attack\") * [Hamas](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamas \"Hamas\") [Mohammed Sinwar](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohammed_Sinwar \"Mohammed Sinwar\") [**X**](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Gaza_European_Hospital_strikes \"2025 Gaza European Hospital strikes\") * [Hamas](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamas \"Hamas\") [Izz al-Din al-Haddad](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Izz_al-Din_al-Haddad \"Izz al-Din al-Haddad\") [**X**](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Izz_al-Din_al-Haddad#Assassination \"Izz al-Din al-Haddad\") * [Hamas](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamas \"Hamas\") [Mohammed Odeh](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohammed_Odeh_(Palestinian_militant) \"Mohammed Odeh (Palestinian militant)\") [**X**](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohammed_Odeh_(Palestinian_militant)#Assassination \"Mohammed Odeh (Palestinian militant)\") * [Hamas](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamas \"Hamas\") [Khalil al-Hayya](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khalil_al-Hayya \"Khalil al-Hayya\") | * [Israel](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israel \"Israel\") [Benjamin Netanyahu](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benjamin_Netanyahu \"Benjamin Netanyahu\") * [Israel](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israel \"Israel\") [Yoav Gallant](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoav_Gallant \"Yoav Gallant\") * [Israel](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israel \"Israel\") [Israel Katz](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israel_Katz \"Israel Katz\") * [Israel](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israel \"Israel\") [Benny Gantz](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benny_Gantz \"Benny Gantz\") * [Israel](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israel \"Israel\") [Eyal Zamir](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eyal_Zamir \"Eyal Zamir\") |\n| Units involved | |\n| See [Order of battle](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaza_war_order_of_battle \"Gaza war order of battle\") | |\n| Strength | |\n| [Hamas](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamas \"Hamas\") 20,000–40,000[[6]](#cite_note-CIA_fact_book-8)[[7]](#cite_note-9) | [Israel](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israel \"Israel\") 529,500[[c]](#cite_note-12) |\n| [Casualties and losses](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casualties_of_the_Gaza_war \"Casualties of the Gaza war\") | |\n| **Gaza Strip:**   * 81,066+ reported killed[[d]](#cite_note-gazamoh-16) ([\"indirect\" deaths](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaza_genocide#Indirect_deaths \"Gaza genocide\") may be many times higher)[[13]](#cite_note-GDS2008-17)[[14]](#cite_note-18) * 173,514+ wounded[[11]](#cite_note-deaths-14) * 12,000+ detained[[15]](#cite_note-19)   **Israel:**[[e]](#cite_note-20)   * 1,609 militants killed[[16]](#cite_note-mako_militants_killed-21) and 200+ captured[[17]](#cite_note-strength1-22)  ---  **Total killed:** 83,287+[[f]](#cite_note-23) | **Total:**   * 800+ civilians killed[[18]](#cite_note-israeli-civilian-casualties-24) * 1,154+ [security personnel](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israeli_security_forces \"Israeli security forces\") killed[[19]](#cite_note-25)[[20]](#cite_note-wp-hostagecount-26)[[21]](#cite_note-ynet-idf-27) * 13,500+ civilians and soldiers wounded[[g]](#cite_note-30) * 251 captured or abducted (85 killed)[[20]](#cite_note-wp-hostagecount-26)  ---  **Total killed:** 2,039+ |\n\nThe **Gaza war**[[h]](#cite_note-31) is an armed conflict in the [Gaza Strip](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaza_Strip \"Gaza Strip\") and [Israel](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israel \"Israel\"), fought as part of the unresolved [Israeli–Palestinian](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israeli%E2%80%93Palestinian_conflict \"Israeli–Palestinian conflict\") and [Gaza–Israel](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaza%E2%80%93Israel_conflict \"Gaza–Israel conflict\") conflicts. The war began on 7 October 2023, when the Palestinian militant group [Hamas](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hamas \"Hamas\") led [a surprise attack on Israel](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/October_7_attacks \"October 7 attacks\"), in which 1,195 [Israelis](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israelis \"Israelis\") and foreign nationals were killed and [251 were taken hostage](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaza_war_hostage_crisis \"Gaza war hostage crisis\"). Since the start of the Israeli offensive that followed, over 73,000 [Palestinians](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palestinians \"Palestinians\") in Gaza [have been killed](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casualties_of_the_Gaza_war \"Casualties of the Gaza war\");[[11]](#cite_note-deaths-14)[[24]](#cite_note-32)[[25]](#cite_note-33) several studies in *[The Lancet](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Lancet \"The Lancet\")* indicate this figure is likely a significant undercount.[[26]](#cite_note-Lancet2025-34)[[27]](#cite_note-35)[[28]](#cite_note-36)[[29]](#cite_note-37) Many scholarly sources and international organizations—including [UN bodies](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations \"United Nations\"), [NGOs](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-governmental_organization \"Non-governmental organization\"), and the [International Association of Genocide Scholars](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Association_of_Genocide_Scholars \"International Association of Genocide Scholars\") have concluded that Israel's actions in [Gaza constitute genocide](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaza_genocide \"Gaza genocide\") under international law.[[i]](#cite_note-43) Several states have also [acknowledged that genocide is occurring](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaza_genocide_recognition \"Gaza genocide recognition\") and have supported legal proceedings before the [International Court of Justice](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Court_of_Justice \"International Court of Justice\"). Israel and its supporters, including the United States, [deny](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaza_genocide_denial \"Gaza genocide denial\") that genocide has occurred.[[35]](#cite_note-44)[[36]](#cite_note-45)[[37]](#cite_note-46)\n\nFollowing the 7 October attacks, Israel launched a [bombing campaign](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israeli_bombing_of_the_Gaza_Strip \"Israeli bombing of the Gaza Strip\") and later invaded Gaza on 27 October after clearing militants from its territory. [Israeli forces](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israeli_forces \"Israeli forces\") launched several campaigns, including the [Rafah offensive](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rafah_offensive \"Rafah offensive\"), three battles fought around [Khan Yunis](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khan_Yunis \"Khan Yunis\"), and the [siege of North Gaza](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_North_Gaza \"Siege of North Gaza\"), culminating in a 2025 [offensive in Gaza City](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2025_Gaza_City_offensive \"2025 Gaza City offensive\"). They have assassinated Hamas leaders inside and outside of Gaza. A [2023 ceasefire](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_Gaza_war_ceasefire \"2023 Gaza war ceasefire\") broke down, and a [second ceasefire in January 2025](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/January_2025_Gaza_war_ceasefire \"January 2025 Gaza war ceasefire\") ended with [a surprise attack by Israel](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/March_2025_Israeli_attacks_on_the_Gaza_Strip \"March 2025 Israeli attacks on the Gaza Strip\") in March. A third ceasefire came into effect on 10 October after Israel and Hamas agreed to phase one of a [US-backed peace plan](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaza_peace_plan \"Gaza peace plan\").[[38]](#cite_note-theguardian20251009-47)[[39]](#cite_note-wsj20251010-48) Hamas announced the resignation of [its civil administration](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaza_Strip_under_Hamas \"Gaza Strip under Hamas\") under the peace plan on 6 July 2026.[[40]](#cite_note-49)\n\nThe war has resulted in [significant humanitarian costs](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaza_humanitarian_crisis \"Gaza humanitarian crisis\"). A [tightened blockade by Israel](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Israeli_blockade_of_the_Gaza_Strip_(2023%E2%80%93present) \"Israeli blockade of the Gaza Strip (2023–present)\") cut off basic necessities, which led to a [partial famine](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gaza_Strip_famine \"Gaza Strip famine\").[[41]](#cite_note-50)[[42]](#cite_note-RIFGS-51)[[43]](#cite_note-52)[[44]](#cite_note-53) Around 90% of Gaza's civilian infrastructure has been destroyed and essential services, including water, electricity, and sanitation, have been severely disrupted;[[45]](#cite_note-54) large parts are uninhabitable,[[46]](#cite_note-amnesty20241205-55) with most hospitals, [religious and cultural landmarks](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Destruction_of_cultural_heritage_during_the_Israeli_invasion_of_the_Gaza_Strip \"Destruction of cultural heritage during the Israeli invasion of the Gaza Strip\"),[[47]](#cite_note-Ahmed-2024\n\n<error>Content truncated. Call the fetch tool with a start_index of 12000 to get more content.</error>"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
